+## `hist-rows.txt` format, and freezing a finished term
+
+One row per offering, pipe-separated:
+
+```
+term|name|loc|time|dow|kind|firstDate|lastDate|occ|enrolled|capacity|waitlist|enrolledAtStart[|x]
+```
+
+`kind` is `s` (weekly series), `c` (camp) or `o` (one-off). The optional 14th field `x` marks
+a section **cancelled** that term. Cancelled rows stay in the file on purpose: the term view
+shows a Cancelled tile ("N · seats withdrawn"), and Analytics leaves them out of every fill rate
+and counts them separately (tile + "Compare two terms").
+
+**When a term ends and is frozen into this file, every section in that term's `CANCELLED` list
+must be written with `x` and the capacity it had *before* it was cancelled.** Sawyer cancels a
+class by setting its capacity to 0 (the calendar then shows `0/0`), so the original seat count
+survives only in the board's own data — the live `RAW` row and `enrollment-snapshots.csv` keep
+it. Copy it from there; do not take a 0 from Sawyer. Spring 2026's three were recorded as 0
+and their counts had to come from Christie (Sep 28, 2026). A row with capacity 0 is dropped at
+load and counts nowhere.
+
 `template.html` is the only file to edit. `site/index.html` is generated, and any hand edit to
 it is lost on the next build. There used to be a second, artifact-flavored build output
 (`enrollment.html`, no auth gate, for the Claude Artifact viewer) — retired once the app moved
